1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,103
By the end of this guide, you will know which of four top race wheels suits your frame, your surface and the way you skate.

2
00:00:08,103 --> 00:00:14,362
We will compare the JUNK Voodoo, the JUNK Road Reaper, the Killer JUNK and the MPC Black Magic.

3
00:00:14,362 --> 00:00:19,896
Choosing a race wheel is one of the most personal decisions in inline speed skating.

4
00:00:19,896 --> 00:00:22,268
Two wheels can look almost the same.

5
00:00:22,268 --> 00:00:26,352
They can roll on the same 608 bearings and fit the same frame.

6
00:00:26,352 --> 00:00:30,898
Yet at race pace, they can feel completely different under your foot.

7
00:00:30,898 --> 00:00:38,870
The hardness figures, the construction details and the race results here all come from the product data for these wheels.

8
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:42,549
First, what all four wheels have in common.

9
00:00:42,549 --> 00:00:44,973
Each one is sold as a set of eight.

10
00:00:44,973 --> 00:00:49,407
That is a full set for a pair of four wheel inline speed frames.

11
00:00:49,407 --> 00:00:52,663
The wheels come on their own, with no bearings.

12
00:00:52,663 --> 00:00:58,689
So whichever you choose, you will also need sixteen 608 bearings and the right spacers.

13
00:00:58,689 --> 00:01:03,469
Before you order, confirm the wheel diameter your frame is built for.

14
00:01:03,469 --> 00:01:07,626
A 110 millimetre wheel needs a frame set up for a 110 wheel.

15
00:01:07,626 --> 00:01:12,405
Once that is settled, the real differences come down to three things.

16
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:17,670
Hardness, hub design, and the character each brand builds into the urethane.

17
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:20,422
Here is the firmness scale.

18
00:01:20,422 --> 00:01:23,995
On the left is Firm, which gives the most grip.

19
00:01:23,995 --> 00:01:29,087
In the middle is XFirm, at 84 to 86A, which balances grip and roll.

20
00:01:29,087 --> 00:01:33,572
On the right is XXFirm, at 86 to 88A, which rolls the most.

21
00:01:33,572 --> 00:01:35,016
The rule is simple.

22
00:01:35,016 --> 00:01:36,840
Softer wheels grip more.

23
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:40,641
Harder wheels roll faster on smooth, dry surfaces.

24
00:01:40,641 --> 00:01:42,237
But there is a catch.

25
00:01:42,237 --> 00:01:46,949
On hard, smooth, dry ground, a harder wheel can start to slip.

26
00:01:46,949 --> 00:01:49,762
That is why grip still matters there.

27
00:01:49,762 --> 00:01:54,398
The right pick depends on how smooth and dry your surface is.

28
00:01:55,098 --> 00:02:00,341
Now, what is actually on the shelf, because this shapes your choice.

29
00:02:00,341 --> 00:02:04,967
A filled green circle means the size or compound is stocked.

30
00:02:04,967 --> 00:02:12,908
Every one of the four wheels comes in both XFirm and XXFirm, so you are never forced into one compound.

31
00:02:12,908 --> 00:02:15,221
Diameter is where they differ.

32
00:02:15,221 --> 00:02:20,386
The Voodoo and the Black Magic come in 90, 100 and 110 millimetres.

33
00:02:20,386 --> 00:02:26,169
That makes them the natural choice on a 3 by 90, 4 by 90 or 4 by 100 frame.

34
00:02:26,169 --> 00:02:30,872
They also suit a junior skater still moving up through sizes.

35
00:02:30,872 --> 00:02:35,497
The Road Reaper and the Killer JUNK are 110 millimetre only.

36
00:02:35,497 --> 00:02:40,046
So they suit skaters already on a full size 4 by 110 frame.

37
00:02:40,746 --> 00:02:42,989
Let us start with the JUNK Voodoo.

38
00:02:42,989 --> 00:02:48,730
It is a pure performance race wheel, with no pigment in either the hub or the urethane.

39
00:02:48,730 --> 00:02:53,876
Nothing is added that could compromise the natural qualities of the materials.

40
00:02:53,876 --> 00:02:58,561
It runs a natural turbo hub that has been re engineered for efficiency.

41
00:02:58,561 --> 00:03:04,697
JUNK also moulds each wheel in a one cavity tool, rather than the usual four cavity approach.

42
00:03:04,697 --> 00:03:09,777
That means tighter quality control, and more consistency from wheel to wheel.

43
00:03:09,777 --> 00:03:18,091
On the ground, it is made for precise control through tight corners and strong speed on the straights, on both road and track.

44
00:03:18,091 --> 00:03:23,765
If you want a consistent, do it all race wheel, the Voodoo is a superb starting point.

45
00:03:24,465 --> 00:03:30,854
Next is the JUNK Road Reaper, one of the most decorated wheels in inline speed skating.

46
00:03:30,854 --> 00:03:36,141
It is a 110 millimetre wheel, the standard large diameter for the sport.

47
00:03:36,141 --> 00:03:39,005
Its record at the top level is serious.

48
00:03:39,005 --> 00:03:44,807
It has won senior and junior men's 100 metre titles at the World Championships.

49
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:47,671
A 100 metre world record was set on it.

50
00:03:47,671 --> 00:03:57,732
And on the distance side, it has won the American Triple Crown of marathon and ultra distance races, including an 87 mile ultra marathon.

51
00:03:57,732 --> 00:04:02,432
From flat out sprints to ultra distance, this wheel has done it.

52
00:04:02,432 --> 00:04:09,702
The XFirm grips more on hard, smooth, dry surfaces, and the XXFirm rolls faster for outright speed.

53
00:04:10,402 --> 00:04:12,381
Here is the quick comparison.

54
00:04:12,381 --> 00:04:17,637
The Voodoo stands out for its pigment free turbo hub and one cavity moulding.

55
00:04:17,637 --> 00:04:19,752
It is the all round race wheel.

56
00:04:19,752 --> 00:04:25,212
The Road Reaper is the decorated 110 millimetre racer, proven at every distance.

57
00:04:25,212 --> 00:04:30,809
The Killer JUNK has a stiffer natural hub, which gives extra momentum in the pack.

58
00:04:30,809 --> 00:04:33,061
It suits pack racing and sprints.

59
00:04:33,061 --> 00:04:40,432
And the Black Magic brings its Soft Heart, Hard Body build on a Black Turbo hub, for grip and roll together.

60
00:04:40,432 --> 00:04:43,844
Each wheel has its own hub and construction story.

61
00:04:43,844 --> 00:04:47,734
Each one earns its place for a slightly different reason.

62
00:04:48,434 --> 00:04:52,706
The Killer JUNK is JUNK's evolution of a legendary race wheel.

63
00:04:52,706 --> 00:04:59,597
It takes a wheel that carried skaters to many victories and world championships, and improves on it.

64
00:04:59,597 --> 00:05:06,832
The headline change is a noticeably stiffer hub, along with several other tweaks over the previous model.

65
00:05:06,832 --> 00:05:12,068
Distance skaters report extra momentum through points and elimination races.

66
00:05:12,068 --> 00:05:16,478
Sprinters get an edge in the closing stages of the 1,000 metres.

67
00:05:16,478 --> 00:05:23,437
Like the Voodoo, it uses a natural hub with no added pigment, and the urethane stays in its raw form.

68
00:05:23,437 --> 00:05:25,229
It is 110 millimetre only.

69
00:05:25,229 --> 00:05:32,946
If you like the JUNK approach but want that stiffer hub feel for the pack and the finish line, this is the pick.

70
00:05:33,646 --> 00:05:37,608
The MPC Black Magic takes a different engineering route.

71
00:05:37,608 --> 00:05:42,135
It is widely regarded as the most successful wheel in the sport.

72
00:05:42,135 --> 00:05:47,865
It broke the 300 metre world record and went under 24 seconds for the first time.

73
00:05:47,865 --> 00:05:54,303
At one World Championships, it won more podium places than all other wheel brands combined.

74
00:05:54,303 --> 00:05:59,962
What sets it apart is MPC's patented technology, known as Soft Heart, Hard Body.

75
00:05:59,962 --> 00:06:04,560
A softer inner ring sits inside a harder outer layer of urethane.

76
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:07,673
The soft heart lets the wheel flex for grip.

77
00:06:07,673 --> 00:06:11,422
The hard body keeps it rolling fast and lasting long.

78
00:06:11,422 --> 00:06:16,162
It sits on a stiffer Black Turbo hub, which adds roll and response.

79
00:06:16,862 --> 00:06:19,048
So, which one should you buy?

80
00:06:19,048 --> 00:06:20,857
Work through four steps.

81
00:06:20,857 --> 00:06:25,305
Frame size first, then surface, then discipline, then feel.

82
00:06:25,305 --> 00:06:28,094
Frame size narrows the field fastest.

83
00:06:28,094 --> 00:06:32,089
On a 4 by 110 frame, all four wheels are open to you.

84
00:06:32,089 --> 00:06:39,401
On a 3 by 90, 4 by 90 or 4 by 100 frame, you are choosing between the Voodoo and the Black Magic.

85
00:06:39,401 --> 00:06:40,607
Next is surface.

86
00:06:40,607 --> 00:06:46,939
On a hard, smooth, dry track or road, XFirm gives you grip while still rolling well.

87
00:06:46,939 --> 00:06:52,592
That makes it the sensible default for most Indian rinks and road circuits.

88
00:06:52,592 --> 00:06:59,451
If you skate flat out on very smooth, dry ground and chase top speed, XXFirm rolls fastest.

89
00:07:00,151 --> 00:07:01,921
One last practical point.

90
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:06,099
This diagram shows one foot, with four wheels on the frame.

91
00:07:06,099 --> 00:07:10,559
Each wheel takes two 608 bearings, with a spacer in the middle.

92
00:07:10,559 --> 00:07:13,320
A set of eight wheels covers both feet.

93
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:17,568
So you need sixteen 608 bearings in total, plus the spacers.

94
00:07:17,568 --> 00:07:19,692
Plan for those when you order.

95
00:07:19,692 --> 00:07:23,303
And once your wheels are on, rotate them regularly.

96
00:07:23,303 --> 00:07:26,914
It keeps the wear even and makes a set last longer.

97
00:07:26,914 --> 00:07:32,790
How long a set lasts depends on your weight, your surface and how often you rotate.

98
00:07:33,490 --> 00:07:37,349
Any of these four wheels will serve a serious skater well.

99
00:07:37,349 --> 00:07:40,476
The Voodoo is the pure, consistent all rounder.

100
00:07:40,476 --> 00:07:44,336
The Road Reaper is the decorated racer for every distance.

101
00:07:44,336 --> 00:07:48,527
The Killer JUNK adds a stiffer hub for pack racing and sprints.

102
00:07:48,527 --> 00:07:52,652
And the Black Magic brings its Soft Heart, Hard Body layering.

103
00:07:52,652 --> 00:07:54,915
The differences are real but fine.

104
00:07:54,915 --> 00:07:58,108
So trust your frame, your surface and your feel.

105
00:07:58,108 --> 00:08:03,298
The full guide is on the LiveLica blog, with every size and compound laid out.

106
00:08:03,298 --> 00:08:05,361
The link is in the description.
